{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444474-v20-vampire-the-masquerade-20th-anniversary-setting-generator","id":1444474,"title":"[V20] 'Vampire, the Masquerade 20th anniversary' Setting Generator","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-18T02:58:29-07:00","id":1444474,"title":"[V20] 'Vampire, the Masquerade 20th anniversary' Setting Generator","content":"Hello, everybody!<br /> <br /> The following can be considered the greatest of all heresies, a mere anecdote or anything in the middle. I have created a (mega)table for the free program <a href=\"https://www.nbos.com/products/inspiration-pad-pro\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Inspiration Pad Pro</b></a> that generates an alternate setting for <i>Vampire, the Masquerade 20<sup>th</sup> Anniversary Edition</i>. Those who are also members of rpg.net probably will know that already, as this begun some weeks ago, and its evolution is described <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/vampire-the-masquerade-randomizing-the-metaplot.879319/\" target=\"_blank\">in this thread of that forum</a>. From its humble beginnings, this generator has turned into a monstrosity that regurgitates a wall of text of (more or less) 2500 words. That\u2019s 5 pages in Word (with an Arial 11 font) when I copy&amp;paste it directly in that program. There will be grammar inconsistencies in the text, because sometimes the fragments don't fit perfectly when joined\u2026but also because English is not my first language (and this also explains the presence of typos here and there). <br /> <br /> So, in each new setting, the composition of the main factions is both similar and different than the original one. For example, in the Camarilla, there will those who rule, those who (more or less) support them, those who want to usurp them, those who are always protesting, those who stay on the sidelines, those whose deal deal nobody knows and those who are on they way out. But each of these roles will be occupied by a random clan. The same is applied to the Sabbat and the Independents. Also, the geopolitical aspects of the setting are randomly generated: sometimes, one faction will be more powerful in some areas of the USA, and sometimes it will be in others. A bunch of Camarilla and two Sabbat cities are described, too, showing their actual situation and including some plot-seeds. All of them at random, of course.<br /> <br /> And I am talking about \u2018<i>Camarilla\u2019</i>\u2019 \u2026but, as a matter of fact, the names of the factions are also randomly generated...as the names of the different positions of power (a Prince may still be a Prince, but it can also be a President, General or who knows what). I can not even imagine how are the probabilities to obtain the <i>original </i>setting as a result at this point\u2026but I suspect that they are astronomically low!<br /> <br /> The most recent version of the generator (9.01) can be downloaded <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/16CukpVJnRv_ZXSdLcTx2ab4bKQvDSw_-/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">from this link</a>. Also, in <a href=\"https://ucmeumm.blogspot.com/p/vampire-masquerade-setting-generator_18.html\" target=\"_blank\">this link</a> there is a full examples of settings generated with the most recent version. And\u2026this generator is may keep growing with time. It's just about building on what's already done, after all\u2026<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26787-dr-gerald-ravenpie","name":"Dr. Gerald Ravenpie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26787_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T03:02:36-07:00","id":1444475,"title":"","content":"As example, I have generated one setting (different from the one I quoted before), and I will quote some parts of it.<br /> <br /> The following is the part concerning the Camarilla (or, in this case, the <i>Secret Alliance</i>) composition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Funded after the disarray of the <i>Moaner Revolt</i>, which led to the raging claws of the lupines, the main organization of the vampires receives the name of <b>the Secret Alliance</b>, and its people attempt to protect the Masquerade as top priority. This organization is led by the Tremere , with a certain sense of detachment. Those Tremere trust the collaboration of the Lasombra and the later are more or less sincere in that. However, the Tzimisce seek to seize the Tremere's \u2018rights\u2019 but it's going to be a long-term project. The Giovanni are always putting a spoke in the wheel and they are getting on the Tremere's nerves. Apart from this, the Ravnos mind on their own business they know more than meets the eye. With respect to the Assamite, practically no one knows what are they thinking, but they are making everyone their fools. To finish, the Brujah seem too eager to leave the organization ...and look, they are already gone! Ah, yes, and there is also the <b>Moaner Movement</b>, which makes a lot of noise and are going to mess all up for good, and the stranded <b>Caitiffs</b> with an unknow sire, which are tipically despised but ignored if they keep a low profile...and they are increasingly resentful because of that. </div> </div> </div>The following is one example of the generated cities. It seems that, in this case, the Camarilla\u2026sorry, the Secret Alliance is powerful in Northeast. Ah, yes, and they have selected a <i>militar</i> theme to name their positions. Finally, those \u2018Gossipers\u2019 are the \u2018Harpies\u2019 of this setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The city of <b>Philadelphia</b> is ruled by a Tremere Admiral, whom no one dares to oppose. The Admiral has selected an old ally as Lieutenant, but maybe it is not a decision as as voluntary as it seems; meanwhile, the General staff is formed by everyone who dares, and it has chosen to play by the rules. Lately, an Elder's ghoul accidentally broke the masquerade and heads will roll. Also, several mortals have been vanishingin the last few nights; even if it had no supernatural origin, the Masquerade is suffering because of it. Finally, the cities's most famous members of the Gossipers has been attacked by some unknown supernatural creature and a reward has been offered for the capture of the culprit. </div> </div> </div>There will always, be, also, a not-Chicago, with its own particular seed-plots. And, <i>every time, </i>a disaster will be coming. In this example, the selected city has been no other than...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At last, there is the city of <b>Jersey City</b>: for decades, it has been considered one of the most important cities of the Secret Alliance, and its tale is both epic and frightening. The warnings about the presence of a (missing) Methuselah in disguise, the surreptitious infiltration of a blood cult which threats to destroy the balance of power and an imminent and dreadful attack by lupine which will unite all factions against the common enemy...or they all will be destroyed one by one , are just part of the whole narration of the city\u2019s myth. </div> </div> </div>The following is an example of one of the Independents. Or <i>Unaffiliated</i>, in this case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This way, the Malkavian desire to raise their dark god to make the world burn.This resurrection requires some lost magical ritual, but their plans have hit some kind of a wall. For now, the Secret Alliance wouldn't touch them even with a 10-foot pole...or at least too openly. Meanwhile, the Malkavian treat their antitribu in the Unseen Council as heretics even though their customs are a little similar, so they usually find some common ground. Recently, a prophet in the clan is proclaiming that they are being deluded, and the Elders are asking for their head. </div> </div> </div>And finally, there is a rumours section, which initially were taken from a pool but finally I found a way to make everyone\u2019s dance without stepping on each other toes. Here there are some examples (that <i> Unseen Council </i>is the Sabbat it this setting):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;The Tzimisce suffered a curse by the Tremere. The reckoning is near. &quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The 'Children of Osiris' were vampires who intended to achieve the Golconda, but the Assamite killed them off. A great loss.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Some guys who call themselves 'the Heralds of Skulls' have turned to the Unseen Council because they have pending accounts with the Brujah. I can't wait to see what happens.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A monstrous version of the Malkavian, following the orders of their antidiluvian, is exterminating them mercilessly. One less thing to worry.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Raputin was a Ravnos. Or possibly a Tzimisce. No, wait, he sure was a mage. &quot; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26787-dr-gerald-ravenpie","name":"Dr. Gerald Ravenpie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26787_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T10:26:48-07:00","id":1444675,"title":"","content":"Quick update here: thanks to another user from rpg.net, I have been able to increase the number of selectable USA cities...and also they will be more properly located from a geographical point of view . Even more remarkable, I have moved everything related to this generator a new homepage <a href=\"https://ucmeumm.blogspot.com/p/vampire-masquerade-20th-anniversary.html\" target=\"_blank\">in this link</a>, which will make things easier for me when it comes to notifying updates and the like! This way, an updated 9.02 version is already available to download on that link.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26787-dr-gerald-ravenpie","name":"Dr. Gerald Ravenpie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26787_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T14:14:38-07:00","id":1445116,"title":"","content":"Hi, everybody!<br /> I have uploaded a new version of the generator (9.03) <a href=\"https://ucmeumm.blogspot.com/p/vampire-masquerade-20th-anniversary.html\" target=\"_blank\">to its home page</a>, The results are only a few words longer this time...but those words have taken me a few searches in the net for information : now, every region of the world has eight cities associated with it, of which the generator will choose a few and mention them in the text. For now, it will do just that, mention them ... but my idea is to expand the result with individual descriptions as I did with the cities of the USA. I'm going to take a look at my &quot;<i>The World of Darkness 2nd Edition</i>&quot; manual for ideas. I haven't read it in years ... soit's going to be quite a nostalgic trip!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26787-dr-gerald-ravenpie","name":"Dr. Gerald Ravenpie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26787_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T02:50:15-07:00","id":1445800,"title":"","content":"A new update! There is now a <a href=\"https://ucmeumm.blogspot.com/p/vampire-masquerade-20th-anniversary.html\" target=\"_blank\">10.01 version</a> of the generator, which includes a description of two not-Camarilla cities in the world (following the same template than those in the USA) and a thid more peculiar one. The pool of plot-seeds has been exapend, because I decided that an expanded common pool for both USA and non-USA cities was a better option than creating a separate one (Kindred are at each other throats without distinction of country or region, after all). And, finally, not-Camarilla and not-Sabbat are at war in some place of the world...and this war is now being described. The generator now makes a text with a 3000-ish word count: at this rate, it's going to reach the thin-splatbook category any of these days...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26787-dr-gerald-ravenpie","name":"Dr. Gerald Ravenpie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26787_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T02:44:17-07:00","id":1446426,"title":"","content":"Hi, you all!<br /> So I have updated the Generator to a <a href=\"https://ucmeumm.blogspot.com/p/vampire-masquerade-20th-anniversary.html\" target=\"_blank\">11.01 version</a> version and...well, I think I left the &quot;why?&quot; point of view behind a long time ago, and I am more into a &quot;'why not?&quot; attitude. So, I've added to the generator the ability to randomize the disciplines and weaknesses of the clans as well. Or to do that and, in addition, also change their traditional names for names extracted from vampiric folklore. Or you can tell it to use the traditional names without modifying anything, why not? (see? I told you!). In the home page, it's described how to choose one option over another (actually, just select an option from a drop-down menu that now appears at the bottom left).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26787-dr-gerald-ravenpie","name":"Dr. Gerald Ravenpie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26787_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T11:45:49-07:00","id":1446817,"title":"","content":"Hi, again!<br /> <a href=\"https://ucmeumm.blogspot.com/p/vampire-masquerade-20th-anniversary.html\" target=\"_blank\">11.02 Version </a>is up, adding a new configuration option: now, you can select if you want a setting within the 'traditional' regional limits or if you want the whole world to be the playground (or battleground, as it is) for the vampires. The later option, combined with not-standard clan names, will also allow the presence of vampires for new regions (as Japan, Southamerica, Malasya, etc.). The <i>potential</i> presence, at least: as everything, this will be randomized so...who knows what you will get at a given moment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26787-dr-gerald-ravenpie","name":"Dr. Gerald Ravenpie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26787_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T11:59:10-07:00","id":1446819,"title":"","content":"Nobody else seems intrested in saying it, so I'll say it. This is kind of cool... post some more randomly generated ones. Those are fun to read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T01:02:20-07:00","id":1446925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Legendre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444474-v20-vampire-the-masquerade-20th-anniversary-setting-generator?p=1446819#post1446819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody else seems intrested in saying it, so I'll say it. This is kind of cool... post some more randomly generated ones. Those are fun to read.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I'm not posting examples because now they are so big I don't even know if the forum could handle them: they're now in the 3500-word count, and that's 7 pages of text (with an Arial 11 pt font)! Because of that, I upload new examples each time I update the generator (<a href=\"https://ucmeumm.blogspot.com/p/vampire-masquerade-setting-generator_29.html\" target=\"_blank\">here </a>is the most current sample in the 'vanilla' mode...if you could even call that 'vanilla' a this stage; <a href=\"https://ucmeumm.blogspot.com/p/vampire-masquerade-setting-generator_6.html\" target=\"_blank\">here </a>is the most current sample when you go in full wild-mode).<br /> <br /> But, as excerpts of some examples, each one obtained from a different roll...the following is an example of a full random Camarilla (or, ironically, '<i>Sabbat of the Dark</i>', in this case). This one is quite cosmopolite, I say, with vampires originated from Dalmatia, Russia, Philippines, Chile, Spain, China and Italy!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since its beginning, the Sabbat of the Dark has been formed by the members of seven clans. This way, the Sabbat of the Dark is under the command of the <b>Kozlak</b> and they tolerate no open dissent. These Kindred, originating in Dalmatia, have the capabilities of manifesting powers related to fairy magic <i>(Mytherceria)</i>, resisting huge damage <i>(Fortitude)</i> and altering their own bodies in various ways <i>(Protean)</i>. For all that, they go into a frenzy with worrying ease. The Kozlak trust the support of the <b>Eretica</b> but neither party trusts the other. The members of this clan, originating from Russia, have the skills of communicate and interact with spirits <i>(Spiritus)</i>, enduring terrible harm <i>(Fortitude)</i> and hiding without notice <i>(Obfuscate)</i>. On the other hand, it is difficult for them to feed on involuntary objects. Meanwhile, the <b>Dang</b> attempt to seize the Kozlak's government but it's going to be a long-term project. These Kindred, originating fron Philippines, have the powers of summoning and controling the shadows <i>(Obtenebration)</i>, moving at supernatural speeds <i>(Celerity)</i> and dominating the volition of others <i>(Domination)</i>. Nevertheless, they temporarily acquire animal traits when they go into a frenzy.<br /> <br /> Somewhat removed from positions of power, the <b>Piuche</b> are always protesting (and the Kozlak are feed up with them). The Piuche, originating from Chile, have the abilties of manipulating the flow of time around them <i>(Vicissitude</i>, manifesting inhuman forms of perception <i>(Auspex)</i> and altering their own bodies totally or partially <i>(Protean)</i>. Having said that, they must feed on raw flesh, in addition to blood. Apart from all this, the <b>Guajona</b> mind on their own business but are secretly helping the the Dang. These Kindred, originating from Spain, have the faculties of turning their blood into a lethal weapon <i>(Quietus)</i>, employing unnatural forms of perception <i>(Auspex)</i> and projecting a majestic aura <i>(Presence)</i>. Regrettably, they must sleep in the presence of soil from their homeland. With respect to the <b>Jiangshi</b>, no one understands what's their deal, and maybe the Jiangshi neither. These vampires, originating from China, have the capabilities of controlling rot and decomposition <i>(Thanatosis)</i>, employing unnatural methods of perception <i>(Auspex)</i> and acting at supernatural speeds <i>(Celerity)</i>. Alas, they can only feed on a specific type of victim. Last but not least, the <b>Lamia</b> seem too eager to abandon ship and the rest of the clans pray for that night to come. These Kindred, originating from Italia, have the powers of molding the flesh into beautiful or grotesque shapes <i>(Temporis)</i>, overcoming the limits of human might <i>(Potence)</i> and altering their own bodies in various ways <i>(Protean)</i>. Despite that, they only need two intakes to suffer a blood bond. </div> </div> </div>The following is an example of what you can obtain for one of the Independents when you randomice everything. These dudes are have turned out to be scary as heck, not only because of their appearance but because of the type of power they wield...and the rest of the world seems to be fully aware of it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lastly, the <b>Jarracas</b> travel all over the world, and they are viewed as sinister and gloomy doomsayers. The true motive of their travels is that they are on an eternal pilgrimage trip. For now, the Camarilla of the Unseen doesn't touch them even with a 10-foot pole, and the members of this clan are happy with that. Meanwhile, the Jarracas practically never join the Order of the Thirsted, and the original clan doesn't pay attention to those few antitribu. Recently, the Jarracas have inflitrated in Austin, and this movement has been noticed but not answered. The members of this clan, that initially arose in Brazil, have the gifts of using powers related to demons and hell <i>(Daimonion)</i>, dominating the will of others <i>(Domination)</i> and displaying a majestic aura <i>(Presence)</i>. However, they have the appearance of a withered corpse. </div> </div> </div>And the following is an example of one city outside of the USA. The generator, in this case, have decided that the Camarilla is powerful in the West Africa region, so here it is, the largest city in Cameroon!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Douala</b> is ruled by a Piuche Marshal , who is not more than a figure head of some unknown party even if this is a well kept secret. The Marshal would like to change that, but doesn't dare to do it ... yet. In recent times, a local Impundulu Elder has shown quite an interest for a specific mortal as a potential target of Embrace...but that moral seems strangely aware of the situation. Also, a influential Ancilla from the Pijavica has been hold against their will by someone near the Marshal ... and although 'blackmail' is a very ugly word, all of that looked like blackmail. Finally, an Elder's ghoul broke the rules of Neutral Ground and a severe punishment is on the way. </div> </div> </div>By the way, I have uploaded an 11.03 version with only <i>one </i>change: while I were running tests, I give one of the vampiric species an inordinate weight on the tables in order to ensure it was always present in the results ... and I forgot to take that weight off. So, in 11.02, there was a near certainty that the leaders of the Camarilla would be Scottish or Irish vampires. Which is not <i>bad</i>...but if it's predictable then it's not fun!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26787-dr-gerald-ravenpie","name":"Dr. Gerald Ravenpie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26787_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T03:45:26-07:00","id":1447705,"title":"","content":"There is now a <a href=\"https://ucmeumm.blogspot.com/p/vampire-masquerade-20th-anniversary.html\" target=\"_blank\">11.04 Version </a> online. And this time, some Requiem-y thingies have crawled into the generator: there is a new parameter, called 'Disciplines', with four options:<ul><li><b>Basic:</b> Only the disciplines in the V20 manual are taking into account, when required.</li> <li><b>Expanded: </b>Some '<i>deprecated</i>' disciplines (as <i>Kai</i>, <i>Deimos </i>and the like) are added to the pool.</li> <li><b>Alternative:</b> With this option, the clans wil receive disciplines from <i>Vampire, the Requiem (</i>one 'clan', one 'bloodline' and two 'commons' disciplines) instead of the usual three from <i>Vampire, the Masquerade</i>.</li> <li><b>Mixed: </b>Each clan will get three disciplines from the Expanded list...plus a 'bloodline' discipline from <i>Vampire, the Requiem</i>.</li> </ul><br /> So, when used in a totally weird mode, the generator will give settings with excerpts like the following...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since its foundation, the Cursed Camarilla has been formed by the vampires of seven clans. This way, the Cursed Camarilla is under the command of the <b>Dang</b> with laissez faire politics. These Kindred, originating in Philippines, have the skills of molding the flesh into beautiful or grotesque shapes <i>(Vicissitude)</i>, seeing and entering the world of the dead. <i>(Carrefour)</i>, displaying supernatural forms of perception <i>(Auspex)</i> and showing superhuman physical power <i>(Potence)</i>. Though, they must feed on raw flesh, in addition to blood. The Dang trust the assistance of the <b>Jiangshi</b> but it's only a temporary agreement. The Jiangshi, originating from China, have the abilties of mentally manipulating the kinetic energy <i>(Kineticism)</i>, augmented hearing and sound mimicry <i>(Mimetismo)</i>, ruling the will of others <i>(Domination)</i> and hiding beyond human senses <i>(Obfuscate)</i>. Alas, they have a deformed and hideous appearance. However, the <b>Nelapsi</b> are trying to steal the Dang's \u2018rights\u2019 but they are still far from it. The Nelapsi, originating fron Slovakia, have the skills of manifesting Gargolesque features (including flight) <i>(Visceratika)</i>, animating corpses to their bidding <i>(Cattiveria)</i>, enduring huge harm <i>(Fortitude)</i> and vanishing in plain sight <i>(Obfuscate)</i>. For all that, they can't bear to look at the holy objects of any faith. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The <b>Kozlak</b> are part of a tight family with an ancient military tradition, but they will periodically bring new blood.Their seat of power is in a city in Dalmatia, where they control everything from the shadows. Until now, the Cursed Camarilla has not paid much attention to them, but the clan wants to change that...for better or worse. Meanwhile, the Kozlak consider their antitribu in the Unseen Council as heretics even though their customs are very similar, but this makes their animosity even bitter. Recently, some Kozlak seem to be trying to spread to another city in Dalmatia, and they are making good progress. These Kindred have the talents of interacting with the world of ghosts and spectres <i>(Nihilistics)</i>, enhancing fighting preparation while courting <i>(Courtoisie)</i>, performing great feats of might <i>(Potence)</i> and projecting a imposing aura <i>(Presence)</i>. Regrettably, they only need two intakes to suffer a blood bond. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26787-dr-gerald-ravenpie","name":"Dr. Gerald Ravenpie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26787_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T09:23:52-07:00","id":1448232,"title":"","content":"Thanks to the forum member <b>CTPhipps </b>and all those plots that posted in the '<i>101 Street Level and Personal Horror Scenarios'</i> thread, there is now a <a href=\"https://ucmeumm.blogspot.com/p/vampire-masquerade-20th-anniversary.html\" target=\"_blank\">11.05 Version</a>; it hasn't got the big changes of more recent updates, but the pool of plot-seeds is now deep enough to add more <i>cities </i>to the setting (as if they were few!). I'm going to post a couple of examples of them. <b>CTPhipps, </b>if you are reading this...maybe you will find something familiar in these descriptions...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Manchester</b> is a peculiar city where the 'Primis' is another name for the mouth of the local Primogen, which rules jointly. There are two totally antagonistic sides , but the city seems to still work surprisingly well. In recent times, a forsaken ghoul of a Setite Elder is said to be desperately seeking vampiric blood or will die in a few days...and is offering some interesting secrets as paying. Also, one of the Castigator's Bouncers broke the rules of Elysium and the Guardian of the Elysium is trying to clean up the mess. Finally, a local blogosphere figure have been recentily talking about 'the devils in the night'...a little too much for they own good. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Omaha</b> is governed by a Tzimisce Chieftain, who is not more than a figure head of the House of Lords even if this is a well kept secret. The Chieftain graciously accepts it...but maybe it's a ruse. Not long ago, a very young Forsaken is said to be hidding somewhere in the city with a feral dog for only company and the Chieftain wants they to be taken to their presence. Also, an important member of the criminal underworld has been pounded by a group of Reckless and the victim is looking for allies to carry out their vengance. Finally, one of the Castigator's Bouncers broke the rules of Communal Hall and the Guardian of the Communal Hall is totally enraged </div> </div> </div>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26787-dr-gerald-ravenpie","name":"Dr. Gerald Ravenpie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26787_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}